# Short-Term:
    ☐ work-area size should change immediately when the size numeric inputs have their up/down arrows pressed.
    ☐ work areas need option to control how they are resized, defaulting to `expansion` (max point is moved) but also supporting `centered` (grows from center point).
    ☐ gizmos should support having 'labels' which show in-world next to the gizmo handles and which have a predicate based visibility state so the labels are only visible under certain conditions.
         - Default label visibility modes are: 
             - `always`: labels are always visible.
             - `hover`: labels are visible when the gizmo handle is hovered.
             - `selected`: labels are visible when the gizmo handle is selected.
             - `predicate`: labels are visible based on a custom predicate function that determines their visibility.
    ☐ work area wireframe box should be partially visible behind terrain, rendering fully opaque when not occluded, but fading when occluded.
    ☐ BUG: work area wireframes dont render correctly when interacting with clouds (clouds seem to occlude them).
    ☐ BUG: Sometimes horizontal/vertical snapping restriction placement does not work as expected (for slabs?).
    ☐ Snapping indicators to visualize which edges the "build brush" is snapping to.
    ☐ Placement restriction modes (e.g. only placing blocks along a specific plane, such as when you are building a long straight wall or flooring).
    ☐ ISSUE: cant place doors with the build-brush.
    ☐ ISSUE: build-brush cant handle ground-storage item placement, which means certai items like small lanterns cannot be placed via the build-brush.
    ☐ TESTS: create an exhaustive test suite that enumerates all placeable items and blocks from the base game assets and runs their definitions through the build-brush system to ensure compatibility.
        - Test placement logic.
        - Test preview mesh tessellation.
        - Test rotation logic.
        - Test snapping behavior.
        - Test placement restrictions.

